# Phase 3
# Captured 2026-07-28 on Jetson Orin Nano Dev Kit, native-Linux (L4T) side.
# ipc-test/linux-client/linux-client run against the QNX guest booted in
# orin-tcg-qnx-ipc-boot1.log (same guest boot, second of two 101000-frame
# runs -- the first produced the results/hw/orin-ipc-latest.csv row with
# P50=1597157ns; this is the second row, P50=1636269ns). Built natively with
# the L4T system gcc (Ubuntu 11.4.0), no cross-compile:
#
#   cd ipc-test/linux-client && make && ./linux-client 100000 192.168.100.10 1000
#
# 100000 timed iterations (+1000 warm-up, discarded) completed cleanly in
# ~2m40s with zero echo-seq mismatches and zero I/O errors -- the full
# committed iteration count from ipc-test/README.md's Phase-2 plan, achieved
# here on the Phase-3 TCP/br0/virtio-net transport where the Phase-2
# cloud-leg virtio-console transport could not get past a non-deterministic
# stall around iteration 15-35 (see docs/findings.md, 2026-07-28).

